From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:33:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: platform crate, FONTS: as the font folder, no DOS
 volume requesters

vectorcraft-aros-platform holds the AROS calls (Workbench start data, ToolTypes, program drawer, DOS name resolution, error requester) behind a safe API, with host fallbacks.

The font folder list for systems other than macOS and Windows is Linux's; in the -nix path mode each folder names a volume (usr, run, ...) and DOS asked for each one, so vectorcraft-cli info never finished. AROS gets FONTS:. The CLI also sets pr_WindowPtr to -1 at start so that any other probe of a missing volume fails instead of opening a requester.
